proposals.track_verdict:
I propose two narrow, low-prior empirical hypotheses for this track and no architectural ones. Prior art covers interrogating possible future states and reasoning backward from them, both in concept and in mechanism:
- forecasting and passive/policy-conditioned/performative forecasts: FutureSim 2605.15188, Forecast-Dojo 2609.28876, potential outcomes;
- action-conditioned rollout and world models: ITP 2601.08955, plus RAP, WebDreamer and WMA (ids unverified);
- receding-horizon replanning: RAFA, unverified;
- backward requirements: BAR 2505.14079;
- option preservation and irreversibility gates: SafeCommit 2608.04289, LCPI 2609.36741, Heitzig & Potham 2508.00159, DeepRewind 2609.36344, plus relative reachability and AUP (unverified);
- feared-future constraints: SafePred 2602.01725, JANUS 2607.19913, SIMMER 2606.14574;
- persisted triggers and intentions: PM-Bench 2607.12385, PIS 2609.01272, ChronosBench 2601.09382, DeepRewind's per-commitment trigger;
- prevented-future scoring: Metaculus annulment, Boeken 2403.00886, Calibration Is Not Control 2606.21399.

Candidate 1 (prevented-future mis-learning) is the only item the attack-phase steelman kept that is specific to this track. Its value is a reliability finding that applies to any outcome-feedback memory. It is not evidence for temporal architecture, and its strong null (log the action plus one prompt line) may well match.

Candidate 2 (prospection as a relevance probe for reopening) is the cheapest experiment that gates the whole future side of the project. Stage 0 runs on the existing harness and smoke_v1 and can only kill the hypothesis. If it fails, nothing more should be built on the future side.

Rejected, with reasons:
- Persisted simulation-derived obligations, signposts or 'future-mediated relevance': a re-check prompt plus a typed store with dependency links covers it. Forecast-Dojo already shows that carried state cuts cost (median 24%) without improving quality. It is also untestable in the current non-reactive harness.
- Executable future-self copies: no evidence for agents; human studies show persuasion, not better decisions. A matched-budget pre-mortem prompt is the null and must fail first.
- Reflexivity detection: for a single agent it collapses into policy-conditioned forecasting.
- Horizon-dependent representation: a design choice with no evidence behind it.

Citation caveats: several foundational ids are unverified in the local corpus (RAP, WebDreamer, WMA, RAFA, AUP, relative reachability, Perdomo, Liley). Boeken is authenticated via PMLR, not the corpus. Prospection-Guided Retrieval 2605.14177 and KWBench are abstract-only.

